From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@visma.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:28:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drw: fall back to bitmap fonts too for glyphs the first font
 lacks

The fallback pattern asked fontconfig for a scalable font only; where the
only font covering a script is a bitmap one (GNU Unifont as the last
fallback for CJK), every such glyph was drawn as a box.
---
 drw.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drw.c b/drw.c
index c41e6af..5d055be 100644
--- a/drw.c
+++ b/drw.c
@@ -352,7 +352,9 @@ drw_text(Drw *drw, int x, int y, unsigned int w, unsigned int h, unsigned int lp
 
 			fcpattern = FcPatternDuplicate(drw->fonts->pattern);
 			FcPatternAddCharSet(fcpattern, FC_CHARSET, fccharset);
-			FcPatternAddBool(fcpattern, FC_SCALABLE, FcTrue);
+			/* any font that has the glyph, bitmap fonts included (a system
+			 * whose only wide-coverage font is a bitmap one, like Unifont,
+			 * would otherwise show boxes for every glyph the first font lacks) */
 
 			FcConfigSubstitute(NULL, fcpattern, FcMatchPattern);
 			FcDefaultSubstitute(fcpattern);
